«
@@ ============================================================
@@ WBEnv — is a loading within the center of gravity envelope?
@@
@@ Input:  the envelope, a list of { CG weight } points in order
@@         around it; the weight W and the center of gravity CG of the
@@         loading, for instance from WBLoad.
@@ Output: the forward and aft CG limits at the weight W, and whether
@@         CG lies between them, tagged Fwd, Aft and Inside (1 or 0).
@@ The limits are where the horizontal line at W crosses the envelope,
@@ interpolated linearly: the envelope must be convex, as CG envelopes
@@ are. A weight above or below the envelope is an error.
@@ Author & design          : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================

  → env w cg
  «
    { }
    1 env SIZE FOR kk
      env kk GET LIST→ DROP
      env kk env SIZE MOD 1 + GET LIST→ DROP
      → x1 y1 x2 y2
      «
        IF y1 y2 ≠ THEN
          IF w y1 y2 MIN ≥ w y1 y2 MAX ≤ AND THEN
            x1 w y1 - x2 x1 - × y2 y1 - / + +
          END
        END
      »
    NEXT
    → xs
    «
      IF xs SIZE 0 == THEN
        "WBEnv: weight outside the envelope" DOERR
      END
      xs 1 GET DUP
      1 xs SIZE FOR kk
        xs kk GET → xi
        «
          SWAP xi MIN SWAP xi MAX
        »
      NEXT
      → fwd aft
      «
        fwd "Fwd" →TAG
        aft "Aft" →TAG
        IF cg fwd ≥ cg aft ≤ AND THEN 1 ELSE 0 END "Inside" →TAG
      »
    »
  »
»
